course: dictionary
lesson: 5489
title: Latitude: how far north or south
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Latitude tells you how far north or south a place is, measured in degrees. The equator is the imaginary line round the middle of the Earth, and it is at 0 degrees latitude. The North and South Poles are at 90 degrees. «Latitude says how far north or south of the Equator a place is, and longitude says how far east or west of Greenwich in London.»
explain: Lines of latitude are imaginary lines around the Earth, parallel to the equator. «The equator, the Tropic of Cancer, the Tropic of Capricorn and the Arctic Circle are lines of latitude.» They are never tangled up with each other. Each one is a set distance north or south of the equator.
explain: Latitude helps explain climate. Places at low latitudes, close to the equator, are usually hot. Places at high latitudes, close to the poles, are usually cold. «The further from the equator, the lower and weaker the sunlight.» Seas, winds and height also change the weather, so latitude is a clue, not the whole story.
explain: Latitude also has a formal meaning: freedom to choose what to do. «The teacher gave us some latitude with the topic» means you could pick the subject yourself. Check the words around it to know which meaning fits.
fact: Latitude is measured in degrees.
fact: The equator is at 0 degrees latitude, and the poles are at 90 degrees north and south.
fact: Lines of latitude run parallel to the equator, and they go round the Earth.
fact: Places at low latitudes are usually hot, and places at high latitudes are usually cold.
fact: On a map, latitude and longitude together give an exact position: «Cornwall in south-west England lies at about 50° North, 5° West.»
exercise: What is the latitude of the equator? | 180 degrees | 90 degrees | *0 degrees | 45 degrees
exercise: «Latitude says how far north or south of the Equator a place is.» What does latitude tell you? | *How far north or south of the Equator a place is | How far east or west of Greenwich a place is | How old a town is | How tall a mountain is
exercise: Which places are usually hot? | *Places at low latitude, near the equator | Places in the middle of the sea only | Places at high latitude, near the poles | Places with lots of snow all year
test: «In EU5 the far north has cold, harsh locations and the tropics hot ones, which follows latitude quite well.» Why do the far north and the tropics differ in temperature? | Because one is near the sea and the other is not | *Because they are at high and low latitudes, so they get different amounts of sunlight | Because one has more roads | Because people live there
test: Lines of latitude are: | Lines that run north and south through the poles | *Imaginary lines around the Earth, parallel to the equator | Lines that only appear on sea charts | Real roads that go round the world
exam: «The teacher gave us some latitude with the topic.» In this sentence, latitude means: | The distance from the equator in degrees | *Freedom to choose what to do or how to do it | A kind of cold wind | A line on a map that shows the poles
